@startuml
title Earth Defender - System Architecture

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

cloud "DNS / Load Balancer" as DNS

node "Web Server" as WebSrv {
  artifact "Static Assets\n- HTML\n- CSS\n- JavaScript\n- Images" as Assets
}

rectangle "Browser Client\n(Three.js)" as Client {
  component "Game UI & Scene" as UI
  component "Networking Layer\n- WebSocket Client\n- JSON [event,data]\n- Reconnect Logic" as Net
  component "Heartbeat Timer\n- ping(null) every 60s\n- handle pong" as Heartbeat
}

node "Game Server Deployment\n(Erlang/OTP)" as Deploy {
  node "Master Node" as Master {
    component "Room Manager\n- Create/Join Rooms\n- Player Count Tracking" as RoomMgr
    component "WebSocket API\nInbound actions:\n- game_reconnect\n- room_players_number\n- servers_list\n- servers_list_redirect\n- server_error\n- pong" as WSAPI
    component "Server List / Redirect Service" as SvcList
  }
  node "Replica Node (Optional)" as Replica {
    component "Replica Runtime\n- Fault-tolerant standby" as ReplicaRT
  }
}

' Name resolution and static content delivery
Client -[#blue]-> DNS : Resolve web server host
DNS -[#blue]-> WebSrv : A/AAAA/CNAME

Client -[#green]-> WebSrv : HTTP GET /assets
WebSrv -[#green]-> Client : Static content

' Multiplayer runtime over WebSocket
Client -[#red]-> Master : WebSocket over HTTP\nJSON [event,data]
Master -[#red]-> Client : WebSocket JSON [action,data?]

' Fault tolerance / replica topology
Master -[#purple]-> Replica : Fault-tolerance topology\n(replica/standby)

' Internal relations
WSAPI -[hidden]-> RoomMgr
WSAPI -[hidden]-> SvcList

' Constraints and behaviors
note right of Client
- Initiates outbound connections only (no P2P)
- On close: reconnect; on reopen: send reconnect context [room_id, player_id, index]
- Sends ping(null) every 60s; accepts pong
- Parses inbound JSON [action, data?]
end note

note left of Master
Provides to clients:
- servers_list (update list)
- servers_list_redirect (update list, then disconnect)
- room_players_number (update count)
- game_reconnect (re-add ship, continue play)
- server_error (client reload)
- pong (heartbeat response)
end note

note top of Deploy
Non-functional:
- Soft real-time gameplay
- Uses HTTP + WebSocket protocols
- Asynchronous, concurrent messaging
- Supports replica for fault tolerance
end note

note bottom of diagram
Key transports:
- HTTP (static assets)
- WebSocket over HTTP (multiplayer runtime)
Constraints:
- Distributed roles: Browser Client, Web Server, Game Server (Master/Replica)
- No client-to-client connectivity
end note
@enduml
